    "created_at": "2026-01-08T18:10:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-08T18:22:03Z",
    "body": "Looking at this more href is quite tightly embedded into the other properties of that mixin. Now I can envisage this becoming a HyperlinkElementUtils with some algorithms left to the implementing type. Like https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#concept-hyperlink-url-set and https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#update-href I think we could make it so they're implemented in the concrete types and implement an SVG specific version of them. However, I'm not sure what the SVG specific version would be, I guess we'd need to define something ahout looking for xlink:href too? and no browser actually implements this mixin for SVG (despite the spec).\n\nIs this mixin really the best place for us to start with this? Or should we make a new one that shares stuff such as hreflang and download that can be used by SVG and MathML?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
